@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080

### Browse the first page of available cars
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/listings

### Browse with every filter. "all" is the query value for available and sold.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/listings?make=Honda&model=Civic&location=Oakland&minYear=2010&maxYear=2020&minPrice=1000&maxPrice=30000&maxMileage=80000&status=all&page=1

### A page past the end still returns the real total count
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/listings?page=9999

### Listing detail. Replace the id after publishing.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/listings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Photo bytes. Replace the id.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/photos/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Register
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sellers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "displayName": "North Yard Motors",
  "email": "seller@example.com",
  "password": "test-pass-8"
}

### Duplicate email, different letter case
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sellers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "displayName": "North Yard Motors",
  "email": "Seller@Example.com",
  "password": "test-pass-8"
}

### Current seller
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sellers/me

### Sign in
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "seller@example.com",
  "password": "test-pass-8"
}

### Failed sign-in
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "seller@example.com",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### Sign out
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/current

### Publish a listing
# Attach 1 to 10 JPEG, PNG, or WebP files in the photos parts. The first file is the cover.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/listings
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=marketplace

--marketplace
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="make"

Honda
--marketplace
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="model"

Civic
--marketplace
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="year"

2018
--marketplace
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="price"

15000.50
--marketplace
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="mileage"

42000
--marketplace
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="location"

Oakland, CA
--marketplace
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

A clean commuter with a full service history.
--marketplace
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="photos"; filename="civic.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./samples/pixel.png
--marketplace--

### Seller's own listings, including sold cars
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sellers/me/listings?page=1

### Replace listing facts. publishedAt stays the same.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/listings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "make": "Honda",
  "model": "Civic",
  "year": 2018,
  "price": 12345.50,
  "mileage": 42000,
  "location": "Oakland, CA",
  "description": "A clean commuter with a full service history."
}

### Replace photos. Send 1 to 10 files, cover first. Zero files keeps the previous photos.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/listings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/photos
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=marketplace

--marketplace
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="photos"; filename="civic.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./samples/pixel.png
--marketplace--

### Mark the car sold
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/listings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "Sold"
}

### Mark the car available
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/listings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "Available"
}

### Send an inquiry
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/listings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/inquiries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Amina Cole",
  "email": "amina@example.com",
  "phone": "+1 (415) 555-0134",
  "message": "Is the mileage in kilometers, and is the car still available?"
}

### Inquiry on a sold listing
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/listings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/inquiries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Amina Cole",
  "email": "amina@example.com",
  "message": "Is this car still available for a visit?"
}

### Owner inquiry, which is refused
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/listings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/inquiries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "North Yard Motors",
  "email": "seller@example.com",
  "message": "This is my own listing and should be refused."
}

### Owner reads inquiries, newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/listings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/inquiries
